# Phase-4 replay archive — the pending-pickup hold is BOUNDED: a pickup that
# beats its spawn report by more than the 500 ms hold gets exactly one late
# UnknownItem reject (the local optimistic pickup rolls back), and the even
# later spawn report still registers idempotently. End state: the item is back
# in the world, nobody owns it — the old immediate-reject shape, only delayed.
#
# Fossil of: ItemRaceTests.SpawnPickupInflight_SpawnArrivesAfterTheHold_RejectedThenSpawnRegisters
# Mechanism: PendingPickupPump -> ItemService.PumpPendingPickups (PendingPickups.cs)

@0 pickup g1 42 test_item 1.0
@0 fault g1 host delay=700
@0 spawn g1 42 test_item 1.0
@33 expect_no_reject g1
@533 expect reject g1 42 within 500
@533 expect received g1 ItemReject 1
@533 expect no_host_table 42
@733 expect host_table 42 within 500
@733 expect received g1 ItemReject 1
